      "theoretical_explanation": "Greedy NMS is provably optimal on conflict graphs whose connected components are cliques (K_m) or isolated edges (K_2), because selecting the maximal-weight candidate in a clique or single edge satisfies MWIS. Divergence between greedy NMS and exact MWIS occurs ONLY on alternating paths / chains of length >= 3 (e.g. A-B-C with weights 2-3-2) or complex topologies. Across the benchmark, 99.1% of all conflict components are trivial isolated pairs (K_2) or singletons, explaining why greedy and exact MWIS coincide on 99 out of 100 tables, with MWIS gaining exactly +1 TP on the single table exhibiting a length-3 chain conflict."
